{"vid":"UaMb0BkDxCo","source":"UaMb0BkDxCo.en-orig.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.2,"txt":"This is not welding. This is TIG"},{"t":3.3,"txt":"brazing. Hey, welcome to the shop. Today"},{"t":5.2,"txt":"we're going to look at one of the most"},{"t":6.5,"txt":"useful little rods that uh I like to"},{"t":9,"txt":"keep around to use with my TIG welder,"},{"t":11,"txt":"and that is silicon bronze. Now, brazing"},{"t":13.7,"txt":"is different than welding because you"},{"t":16.1,"txt":"don't melt the base metal. See, when"},{"t":17.6,"txt":"you're TIG welding something, you"},{"t":18.9,"txt":"actually melt and create a weld pool"},{"t":21.4,"txt":"within the original material, and then"},{"t":23.4,"txt":"you can add some similar material into"},{"t":25.4,"txt":"it to build it up. Now, with brazing,"},{"t":27.4,"txt":"the intention is not to melt the base"},{"t":29.5,"txt":"metal, but rather to heat it up and"},{"t":31.6,"txt":"provide that shielded argon atmosphere"},{"t":34.2,"txt":"where you can then add the braise alloy"},{"t":37.8,"txt":"to the top. And if you're thinking this"},{"t":39.3,"txt":"sounds a lot like soldering, well, it's"},{"t":42,"txt":"basically the same process except"},{"t":43.8,"txt":"brazing is done with alloys that melt at"},{"t":45.7,"txt":"a higher temperature. There are several"},{"t":47.6,"txt":"different alloys you can use for TIG"},{"t":49.1,"txt":"brazing, but the two that are most"},{"t":50.3,"txt":"common are silicon bronze and aluminum"},{"t":53.1,"txt":"bronze. Today, we're going to use some"},{"t":54.5,"txt":"silicon bronze. Now silicon bronze uh"},{"t":57.8,"txt":"flows a little bit better and I like it"},{"t":60.4,"txt":"for general repair type work. Now you"},{"t":63.7,"txt":"can use it for uh joining bronze alloys,"},{"t":67.6,"txt":"joining them to steel, joining tool"},{"t":69.7,"txt":"steel to carbon steel or stainless steel"},{"t":73,"txt":"or even for cast iron repairs. A lot of"},{"t":75.7,"txt":"times it's a little bit easier than"},{"t":77.8,"txt":"using a cast iron, you know, nickel type"},{"t":80.5,"txt":"filler metal. Now aluminum bronze is a"},{"t":83.7,"txt":"little bit higher strength. that's often"},{"t":85.3,"txt":"used for bearing wear surfaces. It's"},{"t":87.1,"txt":"good for corrosion especially in uh you"},{"t":89.8,"txt":"know marine type applications and so"},{"t":92.6,"txt":"that can be useful too and it can also"},{"t":94.5,"txt":"be used in a lot of the same ways but I"},{"t":96.6,"txt":"think silicon bronze just flows in"},{"t":98.8,"txt":"really nicely and it's pretty easy to"},{"t":100.5,"txt":"use and comes in really handy. Let's"},{"t":103.1,"txt":"take a look at the setup that I'm using"},{"t":104.3,"txt":"here. So I'm using HDP's new"},{"t":106.1,"txt":"Independence 210. I'm running this on DC"},{"t":109.8,"txt":"electro negative, just your uh regular"},{"t":112.3,"txt":"straight polarity. And I'm using a"},{"t":115.8,"txt":"number 10 cup to give some good gas"},{"t":118.4,"txt":"shielding. And my tungsten is just"},{"t":120.3,"txt":"sharpened right to a point. Now, I'm"},{"t":121.9,"txt":"just using a gas cooled torch here"},{"t":123.7,"txt":"today. Now, as far as amperage goes, um"},{"t":126.6,"txt":"I'm just going to leave it set right"},{"t":128,"txt":"around 140 and then control things with"},{"t":130.6,"txt":"my foot pedal and just add heat uh as"},{"t":133.8,"txt":"needed. For the sake of demonstration,"},{"t":135.8,"txt":"we're just working with some mild steel"},{"t":137.2,"txt":"coupons here. And I'm going to tack them"},{"t":138.8,"txt":"together in a lap joint configuration."},{"t":140.8,"txt":"Now, when you're learning fillet welds,"},{"t":142.2,"txt":"I recommend a lap joint over T- joint to"},{"t":144.4,"txt":"start. Not only is it easier to see, but"},{"t":146.3,"txt":"when you weld the front side of a T-"},{"t":147.9,"txt":"joint, the backside is oxidized and so"},{"t":149.9,"txt":"it doesn't run very well. Where with a"},{"t":151.8,"txt":"lap joint, you can flip it over, run the"},{"t":154.1,"txt":"backside, and the oxidation is over"},{"t":155.6,"txt":"there, so the joint is still clean."},{"t":157.4,"txt":"Anyway, there's a little tip for you if"},{"t":158.9,"txt":"you are doing a bunch of practice. But,"},{"t":160.9,"txt":"uh, mostly I like these because they're"},{"t":162.5,"txt":"just a little bit easier to film without"},{"t":164.4,"txt":"that vertical plate getting in the way."},{"t":166.5,"txt":"Now, just for the sake of comparison,"},{"t":168.2,"txt":"let's start off by running a weld with"},{"t":169.8,"txt":"some ER70S6 or regular steel filler"},{"t":172.5,"txt":"wire. Now, I'm starting my weld puddle"},{"t":175.5,"txt":"on the base material. And I'm actually"},{"t":177.8,"txt":"going to form a puddle before I ever get"},{"t":180.1,"txt":"the filler metal involved. And then I'll"},{"t":183.2,"txt":"work my way along. And that filler metal"},{"t":185.1,"txt":"is actually eating into the plate."},{"t":186.6,"txt":"Notice that top edge is just ever so"},{"t":189.2,"txt":"slightly being consumed. You end up with"},{"t":191.9,"txt":"something like this. You could add"},{"t":193.4,"txt":"another pass if you wanted for more"},{"t":195,"txt":"reinforcement, but that's the general"},{"t":196.9,"txt":"idea. Now, let's move to this silicon"},{"t":199.4,"txt":"bronze wire. Now, instead of the copper"},{"t":201.2,"txt":"coated steel, it's this color all the"},{"t":203,"txt":"way through. The hardest part in my"},{"t":205.1,"txt":"opinion of a TIG braise joint is this"},{"t":207.8,"txt":"start. See, I'm trying to heat this base"},{"t":210.1,"txt":"metal up to the point that it'll"},{"t":211.5,"txt":"actually melt the filler metal um"},{"t":213.6,"txt":"without melting it with the arc directly"},{"t":215.4,"txt":"and without melting the base metal. Now,"},{"t":217.8,"txt":"I have to test it a few times. And once"},{"t":219.6,"txt":"I start to get a little bit of material"},{"t":221.5,"txt":"down, then it will flow. And it'll flow"},{"t":224.4,"txt":"and follow right with the heat profile"},{"t":226.8,"txt":"off of that arc. So, once you're off and"},{"t":229.1,"txt":"started, it's very similar to TIG"},{"t":231.3,"txt":"welding, except I'm not melting that"},{"t":233.7,"txt":"base metal. I'm just following along and"},{"t":236.3,"txt":"adding filler metal as I move and that"},{"t":239.2,"txt":"puddle will just track right in front of"},{"t":242.4,"txt":"me. Now, the heat's going to build up as"},{"t":244.2,"txt":"you go along, so you need to speed up a"},{"t":246,"txt":"little or uh back off amperage, just"},{"t":248.1,"txt":"like welding. But you end up with"},{"t":249.5,"txt":"something like this. There's usually a"},{"t":250.9,"txt":"little bit on the surface whenever I run"},{"t":252.9,"txt":"um silicon bronze. But it doesn't take"},{"t":255.1,"txt":"too much to clean up with a wire brush."},{"t":257,"txt":"And it can give a a pretty nice look."},{"t":258.6,"txt":"But mostly it's just really versatile"},{"t":261.1,"txt":"when you need to weld tool steel to mild"},{"t":264.2,"txt":"steel or you don't want to have a lot of"},{"t":265.7,"txt":"distortion on a repair. It's not going"},{"t":267.3,"txt":"to pull and warp as much as you would"},{"t":269.2,"txt":"have with a regular weld. So, it's"},{"t":271.9,"txt":"pretty useful. I think it uh is kind of"},{"t":274.7,"txt":"fun to look at the welds after you cut"},{"t":276.7,"txt":"them apart. So, let's go ahead and"},{"t":278,"txt":"section through this one and just take a"},{"t":280.8,"txt":"look at that brace alloy. You can see"},{"t":282.6,"txt":"it's sitting right on top of those"},{"t":284.8,"txt":"surfaces and doesn't penetrate in really"},{"t":287.8,"txt":"at all. And that's the big difference"},{"t":289,"txt":"with brazing. So, you might wonder, is"},{"t":291.1,"txt":"that just going to pop off of here? So,"},{"t":292.6,"txt":"let's bend it open. Looks like that tack"},{"t":294.6,"txt":"is holding it together a little bit. So,"},{"t":296.2,"txt":"I'm just going to nip through that uh"},{"t":298,"txt":"real fast and then go ahead and bend"},{"t":301.5,"txt":"here and see if that braise alloy will"},{"t":303.9,"txt":"just pull off of the steel. You know,"},{"t":305.4,"txt":"there's no flux or anything on this. A"},{"t":307.2,"txt":"lot cleaner than a torch brace. You can"},{"t":309.1,"txt":"see it failed right through the braise"},{"t":311.4,"txt":"alloy there. So, with the right joint,"},{"t":313.5,"txt":"you can get a lot of strength because"},{"t":315.4,"txt":"you get reinforcement uh through the"},{"t":318.5,"txt":"material it's bonded to. Now, in"},{"t":320.2,"txt":"reality, I don't dig brace all that"},{"t":321.7,"txt":"often, but it has come in pretty handy"},{"t":323.8,"txt":"on several occasions where I need to"},{"t":325.5,"txt":"join something that's dissimilar. Um, I"},{"t":327.9,"txt":"put a copper slip ring on a steel chuck"},{"t":330.6,"txt":"before with it. I've done several"},{"t":332.6,"txt":"repairs, done some cast iron type"},{"t":334.5,"txt":"repairs or uh things like that. So, just"},{"t":337.8,"txt":"a really handy tool to have in the belt."}],"words":[{"t":0.24,"w":"This"},{"t":0.719,"w":"is"},{"t":1.36,"w":"not"},{"t":1.76,"w":"welding."},{"t":2.56,"w":"This"},{"t":2.72,"w":"is"},{"t":2.879,"w":"TIG"},{"t":3.28,"w":"brazing."},{"t":3.919,"w":"Hey,"},{"t":4.24,"w":"welcome"},{"t":4.48,"w":"to"},{"t":4.56,"w":"the"},{"t":4.72,"w":"shop."},{"t":5.04,"w":"Today"},{"t":5.2,"w":"we're"},{"t":5.44,"w":"going"},{"t":5.52,"w":"to"},{"t":5.6,"w":"look"},{"t":5.68,"w":"at"},{"t":5.839,"w":"one"},{"t":6,"w":"of"},{"t":6.08,"w":"the"},{"t":6.24,"w":"most"},{"t":6.48,"w":"useful"},{"t":7.12,"w":"little"},{"t":7.44,"w":"rods"},{"t":7.919,"w":"that"},{"t":8.4,"w":"uh"},{"t":8.559,"w":"I"},{"t":8.72,"w":"like"},{"t":8.88,"w":"to"},{"t":9.04,"w":"keep"},{"t":9.28,"w":"around"},{"t":9.599,"w":"to"},{"t":9.92,"w":"use"},{"t":10.08,"w":"with"},{"t":10.24,"w":"my"},{"t"